{
  "requirement": "The `habeas-requirements` skill MUST tell agents that drafts may be high-level, compound, or incomplete, and that they need not answer every question before review.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has one obligation: the `habeas-requirements` skill must tell agents that drafts may be high-level, compound, or incomplete, and that they need not answer every question before review.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_allows_rough_drafts_before_review]` covers it. The test is marked `{test}` for the subject. It finds the \"Write drafts\" workflow step of the `habeas-requirements` skill with the helpers `step_of` and `step`. It then uses `assert_text` to assert that the step contains two phrases:\n- \"Drafts may be high-level, compound, or incomplete\" covers the first clause: the three permitted kinds of draft.\n- \"Ask the user only what the request can't answer; the review in step 3 finds the rest\" covers the second clause: the agent need not have every question answered before review.\n\nThe helpers are sound. `assert_text` asserts `contains` for every phrase and fails with a label. `step_of` panics if no step contains \"Write drafts\". `step` panics if the step is missing.\n\nThe requirement has no other obligations, such as failure cases, modes or boundaries. A wrong or missing skill text would make the test fail, so I found no gap.",
